The table structure information is (table names): 
['olist_customers', 'olist_sellers', 'olist_order_reviews', 'olist_order_items', 'olist_products', 'olist_geolocation', 'product_category_name_translation', 'olist_orders', 'olist_order_payments', 'olist_products_dataset']
Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• olist_order_payments.payment_type : identify the form of payment used in each payment record.  
• olist_order_payments.order_id : allows us to tie every payment record to a specific order.  
• olist_order_items.order_id : joins the items within an order to the payment(s) made for that order.  
• olist_order_items.product_id : lets us reach the product that was bought.  
• olist_products.product_id : joins to order_items and brings the product’s category.  
• olist_products.product_category_name : gives the original (Portuguese) product‑category label.  
• product_category_name_translation.product_category_name & …_english : optional join if we want the English category label.  

Typical join / filter conditions we will need  
• olist_order_payments.order_id = olist_order_items.order_id  
• olist_order_items.product_id     = olist_products.product_id  
• product_category_name_translation.product_category_name = olist_products.product_category_name  
• GROUP BY product_category_name , payment_type to count payments per method & category.  
• Most‑preferred method per category → highest COUNT(*) of payments.  
• Finally, average the “total number of payments of the most‑preferred method” across all categories.  

Below are ten exploratory→incremental SQLite queries (each limited to 20 rows) that build up to the final result.

```sql
-- 1) Distinct payment methods that exist.
SELECT DISTINCT "payment_type"
FROM "olist_order_payments"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Distinct product‑category names that exist.
SELECT DISTINCT "product_category_name"
FROM "olist_products"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Preview how an order connects to its product category.
SELECT oi."order_id",
       oi."product_id",
       p."product_category_name"
FROM   "olist_order_items"      AS oi
JOIN   "olist_products"         AS p  ON p."product_id" = oi."product_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Bring a payment record together with the category it ultimately paid for.
SELECT op."order_id",
       op."payment_type",
       p."product_category_name"
FROM   "olist_order_payments"   AS op
JOIN   "olist_order_items"      AS oi  ON oi."order_id"  = op."order_id"
JOIN   "olist_products"         AS p   ON p."product_id" = oi."product_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) For one sample category ('beleza_saude'), see the payment‑method split.
SELECT p."product_category_name",
       op."payment_type",
       COUNT(*) AS "num_payments"
FROM   "olist_order_payments"   AS op
JOIN   "olist_order_items"      AS oi  ON oi."order_id"  = op."order_id"
JOIN   "olist_products"         AS p   ON p."product_id" = oi."product_id"
WHERE  p."product_category_name" = 'beleza_saude'
GROUP  BY p."product_category_name", op."payment_type"
ORDER  BY "num_payments" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Counts of payments by (category, payment_type) for many categories.
SELECT p."product_category_name",
       op."payment_type",
       COUNT(*) AS "num_payments"
FROM   "olist_order_payments"   AS op
JOIN   "olist_order_items"      AS oi  ON oi."order_id"  = op."order_id"
JOIN   "olist_products"         AS p   ON p."product_id" = oi."product_id"
GROUP  BY p."product_category_name", op."payment_type"
ORDER  BY p."product_category_name", "num_payments" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Pick, for each category, the most‑preferred (highest‑count) payment method.
SELECT sub."product_category_name",
       sub."payment_type"            AS "most_preferred_method",
       sub."total_payments"
FROM ( SELECT p."product_category_name",
              op."payment_type",
              COUNT(*)                             AS "total_payments",
              RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY p."product_category_name"
                           ORDER BY COUNT(*) DESC) AS "rk"
       FROM   "olist_order_payments"   AS op
       JOIN   "olist_order_items"      AS oi  ON oi."order_id"  = op."order_id"
       JOIN   "olist_products"         AS p   ON p."product_id" = oi."product_id"
       GROUP  BY p."product_category_name", op."payment_type"
     ) AS sub
WHERE sub."rk" = 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Compute the average of the total payments of those preferred methods.
SELECT AVG(sub."total_payments") AS "avg_total_payments_most_preferred"
FROM ( SELECT p."product_category_name",
              op."payment_type",
              COUNT(*)                             AS "total_payments",
              RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY p."product_category_name"
                           ORDER BY COUNT(*) DESC) AS "rk"
       FROM   "olist_order_payments"   AS op
       JOIN   "olist_order_items"      AS oi  ON oi."order_id"  = op."order_id"
       JOIN   "olist_products"         AS p   ON p."product_id" = oi."product_id"
       GROUP  BY p."product_category_name", op."payment_type"
     ) AS sub
WHERE sub."rk" = 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Same as (7) but using the English category names (optional).
SELECT pct."product_category_name_english",
       op."payment_type",
       COUNT(*)                             AS "total_payments",
       RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY pct."product_category_name_english"
                    ORDER BY COUNT(*) DESC) AS "rk"
FROM   "olist_order_payments"              AS op
JOIN   "olist_order_items"                 AS oi   ON oi."order_id"  = op."order_id"
JOIN   "olist_products"                    AS p    ON p."product_id" = oi."product_id"
JOIN   "product_category_name_translation" AS pct  ON pct."product_category_name" = p."product_category_name"
GROUP  BY pct."product_category_name_english", op."payment_type"
ORDER  BY pct."product_category_name_english"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) Final averaged figure using English names.
SELECT AVG(sub."total_payments") AS "avg_total_payments_most_preferred"
FROM ( SELECT pct."product_category_name_english",
              op."payment_type",
              COUNT(*)                             AS "total_payments",
              RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY pct."product_category_name_english"
                           ORDER BY COUNT(*) DESC) AS "rk"
       FROM   "olist_order_payments"              AS op
       JOIN   "olist_order_items"                 AS oi   ON oi."order_id"  = op."order_id"
       JOIN   "olist_products"                    AS p    ON p."product_id" = oi."product_id"
       JOIN   "product_category_name_translation" AS pct  ON pct."product_category_name" = p."product_category_name"
       GROUP  BY pct."product_category_name_english", op."payment_type"
     ) AS sub
WHERE sub."rk" = 1
LIMIT 20;
```
